From 808e4cc2f339ea95422d9ae2d1e059a78d5ddb69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:54:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 24/58] Liveness: benchmark, persisted metrics, model update,
 Android defaults

P5-5, wired through LivenessServiceHolder, LivenessApi (Pigeon) and the
debug page (debug and profile builds; the diagnostics calls are refused
when BuildConfig.LIVENESS_DIAGNOSTICS is false).

Benchmark: runBenchmark(camera) captures 60 frames into memory (the debug
page's preview shows the face), stops the camera, runs AnalyzerBenchmark
on its own thread with the bundled models and each signed test bundle
under files/bench-bundles/, drops the frames and returns the text report
(also logged as "benchmark| " lines). Debug page: "Benchmark" button.

Metrics: after each real-engine session the holder merges its metrics
into LivenessMetricsStore (the fake engine's are not persisted).
metrics() returns the persisted totals and rates as key=value lines;
resetMetrics() clears them. Debug page: Metrics card with Refresh/Reset.

Model update (plan A8): installModelBundle() installs the signed bundle
staged in files/bundle-staging/ (adb push) through ModelStore.install
(verified first, so a bad bundle never touches the store; anti-rollback;
atomic switch), then swaps in a new analyzer factory so the next session
uses it. The first install also installs the bundled models as the
store's base, so rollbackModelBundle() can return to them.
modelStoreStatus() lists the store. Debug page: Model bundle card.

Android analyzer defaults: ANDROID_ANALYZER_DEFAULTS (CPU, 2 intra-op
threads, from the S23 FE benchmark: fastest p50 with exact parity;
XNNPACK is 2x slower, NNAPI 4x, 4 threads oversubscribe) apply when the
config has no mosip.registration.liveness.face.analyzer.intraOpThreads /
.accelerator value; any synced value or override wins, and an invalid
analyzer config falls back to the Android defaults.

Exposure assist (F8): mosip.registration.liveness.face.android.
exposureAssist (default true; "false" turns it off) is applied to each
session's CameraXFrameSource; the session start log shows it. Debug
page: "Exposure assist (dim faces)" switch.

Diagnostics flag: LivenessApi's overrides, detailed logs and camera
timing use LIVENESS_DIAGNOSTICS instead of BuildConfig.DEBUG.

Tests (module, JVM): Android defaults and their precedence, the invalid
config fallback, the exposure assist key, an unsigned bundle leaves the
store untouched, rollback of an empty store, benchmark bundle listing.
Module 73/73, Flutter test/liveness 56/56. Run on the phone: see the
Mosip26 docs/part5-android-benchmark.md.

